# The G₂(2)′ branch of Section 14.7

The concrete binary hexagon collinearity obstruction and its application to
the literal quotient `Uβ/Zβ` are proved in `Endpoint`. The conditional
endpoint constructs the source four-cycle from its two line families and
proves the required distinctness using Lemma 14.7.62(1)'s noncontainments.

Remaining source obligations are the six-dimensional/natural or
seven-dimensional/Weyl module identification (14.7.54), the marked module
and parabolic calculations (14.7.55–57), the critical-pair symmetry
(14.7.58–62), and the construction and transport of the common commutator
family on printed p.1069. Final assembly must discharge all of these from
the original Section 14.7 setup before asserting Theorem 14.7.53.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, combined
manuscript of 1 March 2004, printed pp.1065–1069 (PDF pp.1082–1086).
-/
